@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@ Built around how a Nepali dealership actually runs: Bikram Sambat dates first, N
 
 ## Brand Commitments
 
-- Keep the current look: light theme, dark slate sidebar, blue primary (#2563EB), Manrope for headings/figures, slate neutrals, status pills. Restructuring pages is fine; restyling the app is not.
+- Look (revamped Nov 2026): warm paper canvas (#F6F4EF), warm-black sidebar, deep marine teal accent (#0F766E, the old `blue-*` scale is remapped to it in tailwind.config.js), Bricolage Grotesque for headings/figures, Instrument Sans for body. One calm page entrance per route and a dashboard card stagger; no other ambient motion.
 - Nepali (BS) dates are primary; AD shown on hover.
 - Currency always NPR via the shared formatter.
 
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@ Built around how a Nepali dealership actually runs: Bikram Sambat dates first, N
 
 ## Product Principles
 
-1. Familiar over clever: keep existing page layouts and extend them in place rather than redesigning around a new headline metric.
+1. Familiar over clever: keep existing page layouts and extend them in place. The platform is a catalogue of services (see `frontend/src/utils/modules.js`), not only a dealership tool: each company switches on the services it needs via the first-login business builder (`/welcome`), and the Dashboard summarises every enabled service.
 2. One place per concept: a sale and its sold vehicle are one record; every party (customer, vendor, staff) lives in the Ledger. The Ledger is a book of people (A–Z, open an entry to read it), not a debt tracker — balances are shown, never the headline.
 3. Fast on a phone between customers: the key number and the next action fit the first screen.
 4. Numbers must reconcile: the same figure never disagrees between two pages.
